    69|/** Max wall-clock runtime for the WHOLE job (ms). Independent of per-iteration
    70| * and per-stage limits — a global kill switch so a runaway job can never run
    71| * unbounded. Default 8 minutes; override via input.maxRuntimeMs. */
    72|const DEFAULT_MAX_RUNTIME_MS = 15 * 60_000; // V6.15: 8→15 min — 4 iterations with baseline+post-patch typecheck need more room
    73|/** Max LLM calls per job (across all iterations + attempts). Independent of
    74| * MAX_ITERATIONS — a cost cap so the engine can never burn unbounded tokens. */
    75|const DEFAULT_MAX_LLM_CALLS = MAX_ITERATIONS * MAX_LLM_ATTEMPTS;
    76|/** Max estimated tokens per job (soft cap — tracked from LLM response lengths).
    77| * If the cumulative estimated token count exceeds this, the engine BLOCKS with
    78| * TOKEN_BUDGET_EXCEEDED rather than making another call. 200k is realistic for a
    79| * real coding task with up to 5 iterations (each iteration sends file previews +
    80| * a patch response). The 60k cap was too tight and BLOCKED a legitimate PILOT-3
    81| * change after 4 iterations. */
    82|const DEFAULT_MAX_TOKEN_BUDGET = 400_000;
